      "title": "403(b): eligible schools and tax-exempt organizations",
      "narration": "Rosa works for a public school offering a four-oh-three-b retirement plan. These arrangements also serve eligible tax-exempt organizations, including qualifying organizations under section five-oh-one-c-three. The term tax-sheltered annuity appears in study materials, but permitted funding is not limited to an insurance annuity contract. A qualifying custodial account invested in mutual funds can also be used, and church retirement income accounts have their own permitted structure. Employee salary reductions commonly fund the plan, and employer contributions may also be available. A regular private for-profit employer does not become an eligible four-oh-three-b sponsor merely by choosing an annuity investment. Identify the sponsoring organization before applying the plan label.",
