      "text": "The general employer-size test counts employees receiving at least $5,000 in the preceding year, with specified transition and other exceptions. Standard 3% matching or 2% nonelective designs are not the only current rules: enhanced-limit elections for certain employers can require 4% matching or 3% nonelective contributions. Consult current IRS guidance for the actual year and plan.",
